(2) Nondegenerate quadratic forms and their generalizations.
    A fundamental construction employs nondegenerate quadratic forms over finite fields [60,
    Thm. 2.6]. This construction has been greatly extended to allow the quadratic form to be
    replaced by other functions, including bent and vectorial bent functions [14, 15, 17, 20, 44,
